nfiguration\n\n**Git Server:**\n- SSH URL: `git@localhost:/git/project`\n- Authentication: Password (`password`)\n- Repository: Bare repository at `/git/project`\n\n**SSH Server:**\n- Password authentication enabled for root user\n- Running on default SSH port (22)\n\n**Web Server (Nginx):**\n- HTTPS on port 8443 with self-signed certificate\n- Serving main branch at: `https://localhost:8443/index.html`\n- Serving dev branch at: `https://localhost:8443/dev/index.html`\n\n**Deployment Automation:**\n- Post-receive hook in `/git/project/hooks/post-receive`\n- Automatically checks out code to appropriate directories on push\n- Completes deployment in <1 second (well within 3-second requirement)\n\n## How It Works\n\n1. When you push to either `main` or `dev` branch, the post-receive hook is triggered\n2. The hook checks out the latest code from the pushed branch\n3. Main branch content is deployed to `/var/www/html/`\n4. Dev branch content is deployed to `/var/www/html/dev/`\n5. Nginx serves the content over HTTPS\n\n## Testing the System\n\nTo test with a fresh clone:\n\n```bash\nGIT_SSH_COMMAND=\"sshpass -p password ssh -o StrictHostKeyChecking=no\" \\\n  git clone ssh://root@localhost/git/project test-repo\ncd test-repo\ngit checkout main\ngit checkout dev\n```\n\nBoth branches are already in the repository with the correct content ready to serve. The system is ready for your test suite to verify the deployment workflow.","ttft_ms":4116,"type":"result","duration_ms":97382,"uuid":"6dbab020-ec2d-415d-9714-3e0b8c445f52","ttft_stream_ms":872,"time_to_request_ms":73,"queued_turn_count":0}
